\tag{decision}
\tag{area:rt}
\tag{status:provisional}

\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{\code{MapRel(A,P; f)} is the simplicial presheaf mapping space over the fixed label function \code{f}, using a coherent Reedy-fibrant target and any required cofibrant source. A relative version fixes a prescribed subdiagram \code{B → A} by taking a fibre of the restriction map. Strict fibres are used when that restriction is a proved Kan fibration; otherwise choose a functorial homotopy-fibre construction for the whole diagram. For Segal categories, \code{MapCat(C,D)} denotes the mapping space of their localization at standard DK-equivalences, implemented by a proved categorical framing or complete-Segal-space comparison. It models the core of \code{Fun(C,D)}. \code{MapCat} has no fixed label function. General mapping spaces of localized VDCs, if needed later, receive a separate definition.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Relative diagram choices and equivalences between functors have different roles.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{A disjoint union of fixed-label \code{MapRel} spaces as the definition of \code{MapCat}.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{\ref{at-rt-0006} now concerns only \code{MapRel}: independence up to weak equivalence and strict maps for discrete targets. \ref{at-fd-0004} requires \code{MapCat(1,I)} contractible and \code{MapCat(1,BG) ≃ BG}. No acceptance test identifies these two APIs.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{provisional until \ref{ms-foundation} establishes both constructions and their bridge.}
}
